um didn't care as he felt no pain  or burden as he had been cleansed  because of the immaculate's power he was  filled with pride after seeing her  indescribable form  soon after his vision was blurred white  was all he could see  he could feel hands guide him all while  something sharp slipped under his armor  as he stumbled  and fell onto the icy floor claws  digging into the seams between his flesh  and steel  it's unclear whether he died soon after  this or awoke and  died some other way but from what we  have read it's clear that eardrum is a  man of scars he participated in wars  killed hundreds of people and wanted to  stop the trembling effects that the war  has put on his body so he was offered a  solution which as we know is the  doctrine and the immaculate  upon feeling her energy he was relieved  content and  at peace for the first time in a very  long time he wanted to keep this feeling  as the crypt and its followers were  important to him and he deemed others  unworthy as they didn't have any proof  of worthiness in his eyes none of these  people went through his pains and  struggles so why are they even trying to  be enshrined if they aren't even close  to eardrum in his  level of devoution and worthiness so he  took matters into his own hands and  killed those who didn't belong  as punishment he was deemed unfit and  impure and was outcasted and possibly  killed as a result  another small interesting detail is that  with eardrum we get a secret dialogue  when talking to brother corvid he asks  if you can grant him the same thing you  did with his brothers and sisters which  is finding peace  and in more specific peace and death  this goes back to the statement before  about him killing the weak and with this  information maybe he was killing other  groups as well as the crypt of the  martyr in the seat of infinity groups  have very different religious beliefs  but one thing is common amongst the  shells and that is death  as they've all died in some way but  being killed however is a different  story  and that's one that solomon and teal  happened to share he was actually a  pupil  of the seat of infinity in the beginning  but ended up falling in with the  brigands at some point he learned their  teachings and their way of life  mixing droplets of tar with muddy  spirits drinking heavily all the time  and stumbling from one camp to another  teel and his group would steal things  from others most of it being tar  he claimed that these thieves didn't  know the true potential of the tar  and how it was wasted on them when tia  would drink tar he would see a woman in  his vision  tar has an interesting effect on the  human body where it causes  hallucinations but the seed of infinity  uses it constantly  as they think of it as a way of being  closer to the revered going back to the  story teal saw this woman in his visions  he doesn't know her name but we know her  as sister ganesa  where did you find him family  do not answer just come  closer it's a simple pleasure  to glimpse my beloved even  if he's truly gone some part of him  remains with you  ah a small consolation  but i shall accept this mercy  according to theo every movement she  made she created new copies  each joining and splitting apart at the  same time which ended up forming new  copies  the problem with the tar though is that  it was making his flesh peel off his  skin  and the visions of the sester eventually  disappeared  he still reaches for her in the night  but nothing ever happens  he can still hear her voice even in his  head telling him to go back to the  shrine  constantly but he's concerned that they  may not welcome back a lost pupil such  as himself as we stated earlier  deal at this point was becoming  unrecognizable his kin couldn't even  notice who he was and he was outcasted  when talking with baghdad's teal we get  this secret dialogue that solidifies  this  you've got some nerve showing your face  or what's left of it around her