n where cester ganesa talks  about a heretic who drank too much of  the nectar  and turned into a different being not  even human this is the old prisoner and  a story about him  solomon watched this drinking of the  nectar event occur and was horrified  more audio uncovers more of the  relationship between the two  the two are both on the same page with  religious groups and false truths but as  we uncovered  one went too far where the others stayed  content but says that the knowledge that  they've learned is only afforded by the  silence of  others as everyone is strict in their  beliefs and refuses to listen to others  and who don't agree with them  solomon believes in fate and that it's  not ours to defy but  to fulfill and as we know the old  prisoner doesn't believe in this which  is why he took the glance for himself in  an attempt to ascend  solomon says that everyone is chosen and  even naming us  the unborn solomon knew of our arrival  and knew it would happen as if it was  fate  solomon seemed to not understand fate  though in the beginning of his life  as one day when he was within the  stacked archives inside this archive is  faces of the infinity that are etched  into the stone  stacked in columns weight of this  knowledge could kill a man if he were to  grab one of these tablets in haste as  the rest would fall over and crush him  within the archives there was a tablet  and this had the same name as solomon  the same desires the solomon and the  same scars as him  but he never wrote it so how was that  possible  saying can it even be called history if  it's being written by someone who can  see into the future  just as someone can see into the past  the people he's referring to  are sears people who are supernatural  with insight and can see into the future  solomon claims this stuff to be  unsatisfactory that these seers wield  weapons in things they can't even  understand  they uphold laws that they ignore and  that they've unearthed a tablet  unse